  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">219592 WFP FY22 Ukraine CLOSED Response Cash Based Transfers Refugees and Hosts Moldova</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To contribute to the food security of the population affected by the current conflict in Ukraine, in Moldova
 
 
 
 
 
 To provide conflict-affected population(s) with short-term access to basic needs through the provision of one-off cash-based assistance.
 
 
 
 
 
 Moldovan host families have received assistance in the form of direct cash transfers.
 
 
 
 
 
  
 
 Support with cash transfers to host community and refugees of Ukraine crisis
 
 Extension to 15th July 2022 - Feb 15th 2023 - Amendment 4
 
 amendment A1 &quot;The JPIA is being amended to reflect the cost extension of the agreement until 15 July 2022, in order
 
 to:
 
 &amp;#61623; Provide adequate time to complete the registration and verification of beneficiaries as well as
 
 implementing a second round of cash transfer to 7,000 refugee Host communities in June.
 
 &amp;#61623; Potentially cover an additional caseload of 7000 refugee hosting households through the cash
 
 assistance in the agreed 4 districts
 
 All other clauses of the original agreement remain unchanged.&quot;</narrative>
  </description>
